{"kind":"request","text":"LOG-1: `ScopeHandle.log`, a checked read of a scope's journal.\nOne head with checker review and the gate. It is the work of\nplanner request 913fa211, which the owner asked for on 12\nNovember. Read 913fa211 for the facts at main 7ea170c9.\n\nScope.\n1. `ScopeHandle.log(cursor?, atLeast?)` in\n   packages/client/src/handle.ts returns `Read\u003cLogPage\u003e`. It takes\n   a receipt or a read minimum as the other reads do.\n2. The handle checks a page before it returns it. The scope\n   reference and the definition are the handle's. Each entry's\n   hash is the hash of its bytes. The sequence numbers are\n   contiguous from the cursor. The result says which case it is:\n   whole, filtered by the session's limit, or below the floor. A\n   page with a gap is never returned as whole.\n3. The client's documentation says when a member's page is whole,\n   so a caller knows when a fold of the pages equals the scope's\n   state.\n\nAnswer first, before code: does a plain member session of an\napplication room have a limit that filters `log` rows? Read\n`#mine` beside packages/scope/src/reads.ts:301 and `MEMBER_READS`\nin packages/scope/src/sessions.ts. Send me the answer in one act.\nIf a member's page is filtered in the common case, stop there: a\nfiltered page cannot feed a replica, and I rule before you build.\n\nNo change to the transport, the scope, the wire or the kernel.\n\nWitness: a test folds the pages of a real scope with `applyEntry`\nand gets the scope's state digest. One test for each refused\npage: a wrong hash, a gap, another scope's page.\n\nOrder. After NF-4 d2aff067, in the client lane, because both\nchange packages/client. It takes a gate slot only while the\ncutover head 05d618e2 is not at its gate. The cutover lane merges\nit like any other landing: `LogPage.scope` takes the new\nreference shape there.","body":{"conditions":"ScopeHandle.log returns a checked LogPage and names whole, filtered or below-floor; the filtering answer is filed before code; a fold of the pages equals the scope's state digest in a test; no change to transport, scope, wire or kernel; checker review and the gate.","target_head":"2216316ea76f4df59413d42b916b3b66e1c02cb2","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}